If a clinician considers an opioid-therapy for a patient and the clinician does not provably consider an exit-strategy for the opioid-therapy with the patient then it is recommended that the clinician does not initiate the opioid-therapy.
If a clinician considers an exit-strategy for an opioid-therapy with a patient and the opioid-therapy is unsuccessful for a pain-and-pain-related-function-improvement then the clinician can possibly use the exit-strategy with the patient.
